  "source": "An in-memory store with nested BEGIN, ROLLBACK and COMMIT is a long running practical round. It tests state design more than tricks.",
  "starter": "class KVStore:\n    def __init__(self):\n        pass\n\n    def set(self, key, value):\n        pass\n\n    def get(self, key):\n        pass\n\n    def delete(self, key):\n        pass\n\n    def count(self, value):\n        pass",
  "reference": "from collections import Counter\n\n_MISSING = object()\n\nclass KVStore:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.data = {}\n        self.counts = Counter()\n        self.undo = []          # one list of (key, old value) per open transaction\n\n    def _write(self, key, value):\n        old = self.data.get(key, _MISSING)\n        if self.undo:\n            self.undo[-1].append((key, old))\n        if old is not _MISSING:\n            self.counts[old] -= 1\n        if value is _MISSING:\n            self.data.pop(key, None)\n        else:\n            self.data[key] = value\n            self.counts[value] += 1\n\n    def set(self, key, value):\n        self._write(key, value)\n\n    def get(self, key):\n        return self.data.get(key)\n\n    def delete(self, key):\n        if key not in self.data:\n            return False\n        self._write(key, _MISSING)\n        return True\n\n    def count(self, value):\n        return self.counts[value]\n\n    def begin(self):\n        self.undo.append([])\n\n    def rollback(self):\n        if not self.undo:\n            return False\n        log = self.undo.pop()\n        for key, old in reversed(log):\n            cur = self.data.get(key, _MISSING)\n            if cur is not _MISSING:\n                self.counts[cur] -= 1\n            if old is _MISSING:\n                self.data.pop(key, None)\n            else:\n                self.data[key] = old\n                self.counts[old] += 1\n        return True\n\n    def commit(self):\n        if not self.undo:\n            return False\n        self.undo = []\n        return True",
